Native dependencies are not stored in this repository. scripts/build-git-deps.sh
builds them from hash-pinned upstream sources into
packages/GitKit/Vendor/Clibgit2.xcframework, which is statically linked into the app:

  libgit2 1.9.7    GPL-2.0 with the libgit2 linking exception
                   https://github.com/libgit2/libgit2
  libssh2 1.11.1   BSD-3-Clause      https://libssh2.org
  OpenSSL 3.6.5    Apache-2.0 (libcrypto only)   https://www.openssl.org

libgit2 is linked unmodified, as its linking exception allows. Fixes to it go upstream.

The app also bundles, built from source:

  tree-sitter grammars (JavaScript, TypeScript/TSX, JSON, Python, Swift, CSS, HTML)
                   MIT, vendored by scripts/vendor-grammars.py from hash-pinned releases;
                   each grammar's LICENSE is kept next to its sources
  tree-sitter 0.26.13   MIT   https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter
  omnie-dev-editor-engine   MIT, a fork of Runestone by Simon B. Støvring
                   https://github.com/simonbs/Runestone
  MLX Swift 0.32.3 and mlx-swift-lm 3.32.3   MIT   https://github.com/ml-explore
  swift-transformers 1.3.4   Apache-2.0   https://github.com/huggingface/swift-transformers
  Sucrase 3.35.1   MIT   https://github.com/alangpierce/sucrase
  three.js 0.186.1   MIT   https://threejs.org   (the offline package cache's first entry)
  marked 18.1.0   MIT   https://marked.js.org   (Markdown preview)
  Mermaid 12.1.0   MIT   https://mermaid.js.org   (diagrams in the Markdown preview)
  TypeScript 5.9.3   Apache-2.0   https://www.typescriptlang.org   (offline type checking)
                   its lib .d.ts files carry third-party notices, kept in ThirdPartyNoticeText.txt
  Pyodide 314.0.7   MPL-2.0 (unmodified)   https://github.com/pyodide/pyodide
                   including CPython and its standard library, PSF-2.0   https://www.python.org
                   (both bundled by scripts/vendor-runkit.sh from a pinned lockfile)

The WASI spike (development only) bundles, vendored by scripts/vendor-wasi-spike.py:

  browser_wasi_shim 0.4.2   MIT OR Apache-2.0   https://github.com/bjorn3/browser_wasi_shim
  wasi-testsuite (prebuilt tests)   Apache-2.0   https://github.com/WebAssembly/wasi-testsuite

Model weights are data the user downloads, not part of the app. The spike uses
mlx-community/Qwen2.5-Coder-7B-Instruct-4bit (Apache-2.0, from Qwen).

When iSH-based components (LinuxKit, vendor/ish) are added, the distributed app becomes a
GPLv3 combined work; COPYING.app will then describe that combination (PLAN §27).

